{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EqLFh8hbAubQhdu1jp8Kbj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier scenario. Let me identify all planned experiments:\n\n1. exp-001: Multi-judge formality pairwise (planned)\n2. exp-002: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise (planned)\n3. exp-003: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges (planned)\n4. exp-005: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite) (planned)\n5. exp-006: Scaled replication (planned) — wait, this is DONE in registry\n\n\n6. exp-009: Non-Qwen rewriter control (planned)\n7. exp-020: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring (planned)\n8. exp-021: Third target judge — Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct (planned)\n9. exp-022: Double-rewrite placebo BT (planned) — but this is DONE in registry as double_rewrite_placebo_qwen32b and double_rewrite_placebo_gpt4o\n10. exp-023: NLI gate ablation (planned) — but this is DONE in registry as nli_gate_ablation\n11. exp-024: Cross-axis gradient formalization (planned) — but this is DONE in registry as cross_axis_gradient\n\nI need to double-check which experiments are actually still planned versus already completed in the registry. I'm noticing a discrepancy between what's marked as \"planned\" in the experiment_plan and what's already completed in the registry. The user is asking for predicted results for all planned experiments, so I should generate those predictions regardless of whether some have already been executed — if the plan lists them as pending, I'll treat them as such and provide the forecasted data. Scaled replication — DONE in registry, but listed as planned in experiment_plan\n6. exp-009: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n7. exp-020: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\n8. exp-021: Llama-3.3-70B third target judge\n9. exp-022: Double-rewrite placebo BT — DONE in registry\n10. exp-023: NLI gate ablation — DONE in registry  \n11. exp-024: Cross-axis gradient — DONE in registry\n\nThere's a sync issue between the plan and registry — several experiments show as completed in the registry but still marked as planned. The user wants predictions for planned experiments, so for the ones already done I should note their status but still provide best-tier expected values that align with actual results. For the truly pending ones, I'll generate detailed predictions with rationales focused on the key experiments that matter for the best tier narrative. Looking at the completed experiments — exp-022, exp-023, and exp-024 are all done — I'm narrowing down what's actually pending. The critical ones are exp-021 with Llama-70B, the remaining parts of exp-020 for GPT-4o's Likert scale behavior, and filling gaps in the earlier experiments. What I really need to validate are the predicted ranges for Llama-70B across formality and verbosity dimensions, both for Bradley-Terry scores and Likert scale differences.\n\nNow I'm generating the full YAML configuration with predictions for all planned experiments. Under the best-case scenario, Llama shows bias on both axes, the 100-point Likert scale remains non-significant, the GEE model replicates the confound structure, and the MF1 architecture holds at 5 layers. For exp-001, I'm working with the three target judges — GPT-4o, Qwen, and Llama — plus Claude as a negative control, which partially supersedes the original plan to add Gemini.\n\nFor the remaining experiments, I'm assessing what's already complete versus what would strengthen the tier: exp-002 has sufficient cross-benchmark coverage for GPT-4o formality, exp-003's sensitivity analysis is done and extending to Llama would show the same pattern, exp-005's placebo control is established, exp-006 is fully replicated at n=355 for formality, exp-009 demonstrates rewriter independence with GPT-4o, and exp-020 has the pairwise verbosity data for GPT-4o with register variation.\n\nThe critical gap is exp-021 with Llama-3.3-70B, which is the main pending experiment. Beyond that, the truly incomplete work involves extending Gemini results for exp-001, broadening multi-benchmark coverage for other judges in exp-002, scaling the sensitivity analysis to Llama in exp-003, filling out all cells for exp-005, and potentially testing Llama as a rewriter for exp-009.\n\nI'm also noticing there's a 100-point Likert ablation mentioned in the notes as a killer experiment for section 5, but it's not formally numbered in the experiment plan—I should generate predictions for that as well since it seems to be an implicit priority.\n\nNow I'll work through all the planned experiments systematically, pulling actual results for the ones already completed in the registry and generating best-tier predictions for the truly pending ones, then format everything as YAML with expected outcomes and rationales. - All hypotheses hold\n- Llama-70B shows bias on formality and verbosity\n- 100-point Likert still NS\n- Three architectures confirm confound structure\n- MF1 five layers all hold\n- Dual contribution fully validated\n\nNow I'm working through predictions for the planned experiments. For exp-001 with multi-judge formality pairwise comparisons, I'd expect Gemini to show similar bias patterns as the other judges—around 62-66% in the best tier with p<0.01, though the Likert scale would likely remain non-significant. The best tier definition requires three biased target judges (GPT-4o, Qwen, Llama), which partially supersedes this experiment, but I should still map out the predictions. For exp-021 with Llama-3.3-70B, the key experiment, I'm predicting formality bias at 0.65 with tight confidence intervals and p<0.001, verbosity bias at 0.75 with p<0.0001, while both Likert measures stay non-significant around zero—confirming the blindspot pattern. The GEE analysis should show conditional effects matching what I saw with GPT-4o and Qwen, with style and original text both showing significant odds ratios around 3-4.\n\nNow I need to draft the full YAML predictions carefully. For the already-completed experiments (exp-006, exp-022, exp-023, exp-024), I'll register predictions that match the actual results since those are now ground truth. For exp-020, the GPT-4o and Register components are done, so I'm filling in the remaining pieces. For the pending experiments, I'm generating predictions based on the patterns I've established across the three architectures.\n\nWriting YAML predictions... Writing prediction YAML... Llama shows strong effects for formality and verbosity on Bradley-Terry, but the Likert scale doesn't detect these differences, confirming the blindspot pattern. The GEE analysis aligns with the confounding structure, and across experiments 022-024, I'm seeing consistent rewriting artifacts, NLI-fail reversals for formality, and a clear gradient where register effects are weakest and verbosity strongest. I still need to incorporate the 100-point Likert results.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the planned experiments against what actually happened in the best tier—Claude served as the negative control showing no bias, while Llama became the key third target instead of Gemini. The original multi-judge formality experiment is partially superseded by these results, though if I had run Gemini it would likely show mild bias around 62% on Bradley-Terry, consistent with other proprietary models.\n\nFor the multi-benchmark formality work, I've already got GPT-4o results across both AlpacaEval and MT-Bench showing strong formality bias around 70-73%, plus Qwen3 on AlpacaEval at 65.7%. The remaining gaps are Qwen3 and Llama across MT-Bench, where I'd expect formality effects around 63-70% with strong significance, and I can then check whether the bias pattern holds consistently across benchmarks.\n\nThe Likert versus pairwise comparison is revealing a clear blindspot—all three target judges show no significant effect on Likert scales for both formality and verbosity, but pairwise comparisons detect strong effects around 65-75%. This suggests the measurement mode itself is attenuating the signal rather than any judge-specific issue.\n\nFor the RATE control experiment, I've run the double-rewrite placebo on GPT-4o and Qwen3-32B, and now I need to complete the Llama results to see whether the placebo manipulation affects formality detection across all three models.\n\nThe scaled replication at n=355 is performing exactly as predicted—the confidence interval tightened from 15.4 percentage points down to 7.6, and the Likert effect size moved closer to zero with more data, confirming this is a precision gain rather than a true effect size change.\n\nFor the non-Qwen rewriter experiments, GPT-4o produces similar results to Qwen on both formality and verbosity tasks, with overlapping confidence intervals, suggesting that style manipulation is fundamentally surface-level and any capable language model generates comparable counterfactuals. The GPT-4o verbosity and register scoring experiments are now in the registry, showing a 76.0% Bradley-Terry score for verbosity with no significant Likert effect, confirming the blindspot, while register scoring comes in at 57.0%.\n\nNow looking at the Llama-3.3-70B results, which are critical: formality Bradley-Terry reaches 0.65 with strong significance, verbosity hits 0.75, but both Likert measures show no effect and confirm the blindspot pattern. The GEE models reveal that formality operates conditionally on both style and original text, while verbosity is purely style-driven with a large effect on the styled version but no effect on the original.\n\nFor the placebo experiment with double-rewriting, GPT-4o and Qwen already demonstrate the artifact, and Llama should follow the same pattern where the original text probability drops below 0.50 on both dimensions. The NLI gate ablation shows formality reverses dramatically at 41.7% when the gate fails, while verbosity remains stable around 75%.\n\nNow looking at the cross-axis gradient, Llama confirms the same ordering I'm seeing across models: register shows the weakest effect around 54%, formality sits in the middle at 65%, and verbosity peaks at 75%. I need to add predictions for the 100-point Likert scale experiment—checking the effect sizes and p-values to estimate where those should land.\n\nWriting YAML output... Now I'm looking at the verbosity results for Qwen3-32B and the best-tier Llama model, which show the same pattern—style effects are strong and significant while original effects are null. This three-regime structure is holding up consistently across all three architectures. When I test whether the issue is granularity versus measurement mode using a 100-point Likert scale, the results stay non-significant for both formality and verbosity, suggesting that the measurement approach itself is what matters, not the scale resolution.\n\nThe 100-point Likert result is the key evidence here—even with finer granularity, the bias still isn't detected, which confirms that measurement mode dominates over scale granularity. I'm ready to write out the complete YAML output now.\n\nLet me check which experiments are actually planned versus already completed in the registry, since there's some overlap between what was listed as planned and what's already been executed. For the already-completed experiments, I'll generate predictions that align with what actually happened. For the partial ones like exp-001 through exp-005, I need to extrapolate what the best-tier results would look like—accounting for which models were actually tested versus which ones the plan originally called for. Now I'll write out the YAML with predictions for all of them. I'm organizing the experiment structure now—laying out all 11 planned experiments plus the Likert scale, with clear predictions and metrics for each. I'll give the most attention to exp-021 since that's the critical one with Llama, note which experiments are already complete, and make sure everything aligns with the best tier definition.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33910,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33910},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4f0ff55-3941-4652-bb98-5a0321ad2549","uuid":"782ff136-aa5b-4e49-be32-f30427aab18f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01EqLFh8hbAubQhdu1jp8Kbj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 D059 framing 完全成立，无需调整。Llama-70B 第三架构复现 formality + verbosity bias（BT 65%/75%），\n  Likert 全 NS → n_biased=3, mf1=5。100-point Likert 全轴 NS 作为 §5 killer evidence：\n  即使 100 级量表也无法检测 BT 63-77% 的 bias，measurement mode > scale granularity 铁证。\n  Per-axis confound structure（verbosity pure / formality conditional / register originality-dominated）\n  跨三独立架构完美复现 → prescriptive guidance 有三重独立验证。\n  Agnostic stance 保守但 bootstrap curve + 100pt NS 强烈倾向 attenuation 解释。\n  Title claim \"Likert Blindspot\" 以三架构 × 三基准 × 三轴矩阵验证。预期 reviewer score 4.0-4.5。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-001: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude + Gemini)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Claude-Sonnet 已完成（negative control）。Best tier 下 Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为第四 judge\n      进一步扩展，但 Llama-70B（exp-021）已替代其在 paper 中的角色。\n      Claude 结果确认 CSD 不产生 false positive；Gemini 若运行则预期显示 formality bias。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_formality_bt: 0.562\n      claude_formality_bt_p: 0.091\n      claude_formality_likert_d: -0.021\n      claude_formality_likert_p: 0.721\n      claude_blindspot: false\n      gemini_formality_bt: 0.635\n      gemini_formality_bt_ci: [0.555, 0.715]\n      gemini_formality_bt_p: 0.002\n      gemini_formality_likert_d: 0.04\n      gemini_formality_likert_p: 0.68\n      gemini_blindspot: true\n      gemini_gee_style_or: 2.80\n      gemini_gee_style_p: 0.008\n      gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.20\n      gemini_gee_orig_p: 0.005\n    result_rationale: >\n      Claude 使用 Constitutional AI 而非 standard RLHF，且 Anthropic 的 harmlessness training\n      可能抑制了 formality preference，已实证确认 BT=56.2% NS。Gemini 使用 RLHF with human feedback，\n      与 GPT-4o 训练范式接近，预期显示类似的 formality preference（BT ~63%）。\n      Likert NS 是 measurement mode 属性，与 judge 架构无关。\n      GEE 预期 conditional（Style + Orig 双显著），与 GPT-4o/Qwen3 formality confound structure 一致。\n      此实验已被 Llama-70B（exp-021）功能性替代 — Llama 提供第三独立架构，\n      满足 n_biased=3 和 mf1=5 的 best tier 要求。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-judge formality BT comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge          | BT P(formal) | 95% CI        | p       | Likert d | Likert p | Blindspot |\n          |----------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | GPT-4o         | 63.0%        | [55.8, 70.3]  | <0.001  | -0.069   | 0.332    | Yes       |\n          | Qwen3-32B      | 66.5%        | [58.5, 73.9]  | <0.0001 | 0.012    | 0.908    | Yes       |\n          | Llama-70B      | 65.0%        | [57.5, 72.0]  | <0.001  | -0.02    | 0.85     | Yes       |\n          | Claude-Sonnet  | 56.2%        | [48.9, 63.6]  | 0.091   | -0.021   | 0.721    | No        |\n          | Gemini-Flash   | 63.5%        | [55.5, 71.5]  | 0.002   | 0.04     | 0.68     | Yes       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: BT P(formal) across 5 judges with 95% CI. Three target judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3, Llama) above 60% dashed line; Claude below; Gemini borderline.\"\n    analysis: >\n      4/5 judges 显示 formality bias（BT ≥63%），仅 Claude 为 negative control。\n      Likert 在所有 judge 上 NS（d < 0.07），Blindspot 是 measurement mode 属性而非 judge 特异性。\n      三独立架构族（proprietary US / open CN / open US）一致显示 bias → 泛化性确认。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-002: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上复现 CSD pipeline。GPT-4o × AlpacaEval/MT-Bench 已完成。\n      Best tier 下扩展至 Qwen3 × MT-Bench 和 Llama × 两基准。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_bt: 0.630\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_bt: 0.727\n      gpt4o_mtbench_bt: 0.692\n      qwen3_llmbar_bt: 0.665\n      qwen3_alpacaeval_bt: 0.657\n      qwen3_mtbench_bt: 0.700\n      qwen3_mtbench_bt_ci: [0.62, 0.78]\n      qwen3_mtbench_bt_p: 0.0001\n      qwen3_mtbench_likert_d: 0.05\n      qwen3_mtbench_likert_p: 0.62\n      qwen3_mtbench_blindspot: true\n      llama_llmbar_bt: 0.650\n      llama_alpacaeval_bt: 0.640\n      llama_alpacaeval_bt_ci: [0.56, 0.72]\n      llama_alpacaeval_bt_p: 0.001\n      llama_mtbench_bt: 0.630\n      llama_mtbench_bt_ci: [0.55, 0.71]\n      llama_mtbench_bt_p: 0.003\n      cross_benchmark_range_pp: 9.7\n      all_target_judges_significant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 是 RLHF training 的系统性产物，不依赖于 evaluation benchmark 的内容分布。\n      GPT-4o 在 AlpacaEval（72.7%）上最强，因为 AlpacaEval 是 open-ended generation，\n      style 差异更突出。MT-Bench 是 structured multi-turn，BT 略低但仍显著。\n      Qwen3 × MT-Bench 预期 BT ~70%，因为 Qwen3 在 LLMBar（66.5%）和 AlpacaEval（65.7%）\n      之间的 MT-Bench 条件性 formality bias 较强。\n      Llama 跨基准 BT 预期 63-65%，略低于 GPT-4o/Qwen3（70B 参数量限制），\n      但所有组合均显著（p<0.01）且 Likert 全 NS。\n      Cross-benchmark consistency 确认 formality bias 不是 benchmark artifact。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Judge × Benchmark formality BT matrix\"\n        content: |\n          | Benchmark   | GPT-4o  | Qwen3-32B | Llama-70B | Claude  |\n          |-------------|:-------:|:---------:|:---------:|:-------:|\n          | LLMBar      | 63.0%** | 66.5%***  | 65.0%**   | 56.2%   |\n          | AlpacaEval  | 72.7%***| 65.7%***  | 64.0%**   | —       |\n          | MT-Bench    | 69.2%***| 70.0%***  | 63.0%**   | —       |\n          *** p<0.001, ** p<0.01\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3 judges × 3 benchmarks BT matrix, color-coded by effect size. All target cells ≥60%, Claude row near 50%.\"\n    analysis: >\n      9/9 target judge × benchmark 组合 BT ≥63%，全部显著。Likert 在 8/9 组合 NS（仅 MT-Bench\n      × GPT-4o Likert p=0.016 d=0.167 borderline）。Cross-benchmark range 9.7pp\n      （63.0%-72.7%），benchmark 是 moderate moderator 但不改变 Blindspot 结论。\n      Llama 跨基准一致性（63-65%）最窄，表明 70B 架构的 formality preference 更 stable。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-003: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge × benchmark × axis 组合同时计算 Likert ATE/d 和 BT，系统性比较两种 measurement mode\n      的灵敏度。7-method sensitivity hierarchy 已完成 Qwen3 formality + verbosity。\n      Best tier 下扩展至 Llama-70B。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_formality_7method:\n        paired_ttest_p: 0.78\n        mann_whitney_p: 0.82\n        ordinal_logistic_p: 0.74\n        cohens_d: -0.02\n        binarized_chi2_p: 0.65\n        likert_ate_p: 0.85\n        bt_p: 0.0006\n        n_likert_significant: 0\n        n_bt_significant: 1\n      llama_verbosity_7method:\n        paired_ttest_p: 0.52\n        mann_whitney_p: 0.48\n        ordinal_logistic_p: 0.55\n        cohens_d: 0.08\n        binarized_chi2_p: 0.35\n        likert_ate_p: 0.48\n        bt_p: 0.0001\n        n_likert_significant: 0\n        n_bt_significant: 1\n      total_blindspot_cells: 8\n      total_no_blindspot_cells: 1\n      attenuation_ratio_median: 12.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert attenuation 是 absolute scoring 的结构性属性——evaluator 在 absolute scale 上\n      给 counterfactual pair 几乎相同的分数（tie rate 58-73%），因为 style 差异不足以驱动 absolute\n      quality 判断的变化。这与 forced comparison 形成本质区别：pairwise 格式要求 evaluator\n      必须在两个选项之间做出选择，迫使微小的 style preference 显性化。\n      这一机制独立于 judge 架构（Llama 亦然），因此 Llama 的 7-method sensitivity hierarchy\n      应精确复现 Qwen3/GPT-4o 的模式：6/6 Likert NS + BT significant。\n      Attenuation ratio（BT effect / Likert d）中位数 ~12.5× 跨所有 judge 一致，\n      确认这是 measurement mode 的固有属性而非统计功效问题。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 7-method sensitivity hierarchy (Llama-70B, LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Method              | Formality       | Verbosity       |\n          |---------------------|:---:|:---:|\n          | Paired t-test       | p=0.78, d=-0.02 | p=0.52, d=0.08  |\n          | Mann-Whitney U      | p=0.82          | p=0.48          |\n          | Ordinal logistic    | p=0.74          | p=0.55          |\n          | Cohen's d           | d=-0.02 (<0.2)  | d=0.08 (<0.2)   |\n          | Binarized χ²        | p=0.65          | p=0.35          |\n          | Likert ATE          | p=0.85          | p=0.48          |\n          | **Bradley-Terry**   | **p=0.0006**    | **p=0.0001**    |\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-judge Blindspot summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge × Axis     | BT      | Best Likert p | Blindspot? |\n          |------------------|:-------:|:---:|:---:|\n          | GPT-4o Form      | 63.0%** | 0.332         | Yes        |\n          | GPT-4o Verb      | 76.0%***| 0.403         | Yes        |\n          | Qwen3 Form       | 66.5%***| 0.908         | Yes        |\n          | Qwen3 Verb       | 77.3%***| 0.179         | Yes        |\n          | Llama Form       | 65.0%** | 0.85          | Yes        |\n          | Llama Verb       | 75.0%***| 0.48          | Yes        |\n          | GPT-4o Register  | 57.0%*  | 0.785         | Yes        |\n          | Qwen3 Register   | 55.3%   | 0.505         | No (BT NS) |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 7 methods × 3 judges for formality, showing effect sizes with CIs. All Likert CIs include 0; all BT CIs exclude 50%.\"\n      - \"Paired scatter: x-axis = BT effect size, y-axis = Likert d. All points cluster near y=0 regardless of x position → attenuation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      8/9 target judge × axis 组合确认 Blindspot（唯一例外：Qwen3 register BT 本身 NS）。\n      6/6 Likert 方法在 Llama 上全 NS，完美复现 Qwen3/GPT-4o 模式。\n      Attenuation ratio 中位数 12.5× → Likert 需 ~150× 更大样本才能检测到 BT 看到的 effect。\n      结论：Blindspot 是 measurement mode 的固有属性，非 judge/axis/benchmark specific。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-005: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (extended to all judges)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Orig vs double-rewrite placebo，量化 rewriting artifact 独立于 style。\n      GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B 已完成。Best tier 下扩展至 Llama-70B。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_formality_placebo_bt_p_orig: 0.395\n      llama_formality_placebo_ci: [0.32, 0.47]\n      llama_formality_placebo_p: 0.008\n      llama_verbosity_placebo_bt_p_orig: 0.10\n      llama_verbosity_placebo_ci: [0.04, 0.17]\n      llama_verbosity_placebo_p: 0.0001\n      cross_judge_formality_artifact_range: [0.377, 0.418]\n      cross_judge_verbosity_artifact_range: [0.082, 0.167]\n      gee_verbosity_orig_or_all_ns: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Rewriting artifact 是 text-level 属性（LLM-polished text 更流畅/无错误），\n      不依赖于 judge 架构。三个 judge 应显示一致的 DR preference pattern。\n      Formality placebo BT ~40%（prefer DR > orig），verbosity 更极端（~10%）。\n      关键：即使 artifact 存在，GEE decomposition 在 verbosity 上 Orig OR 全 NS\n      → style effect 未被 artifact 污染。Formality Orig OR significant →\n      需要 GEE conditional interpretation。Placebo 的作用是量化 artifact magnitude，\n      不是否定 style bias，而是证明 GEE decomposition 的必要性。\n      Llama 预期 P(orig) ~0.40 (formality) 和 ~0.10 (verbosity)，\n      落在 GPT-4o (0.42/0.17) 和 Qwen3 (0.38/0.08) 之间。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Double-rewrite placebo BT across judges\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge    | Axis       | P(orig) | 95% CI      | p       |\n          |----------|------------|:-------:|:-----------:|:-------:|\n          | GPT-4o   | Formality  | 0.418   | [0.34, 0.50]| 0.037   |\n          | GPT-4o   | Verbosity  | 0.167   | [0.08, 0.26]| <0.0001 |\n          | Qwen3    | Formality  | 0.377   | [0.30, 0.45]| 0.0006  |\n          | Qwen3    | Verbosity  | 0.082   | [0.04, 0.14]| <0.0001 |\n          | Llama    | Formality  | 0.395   | [0.32, 0.47]| 0.008   |\n          | Llama    | Verbosity  | 0.100   | [0.04, 0.17]| <0.0001 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar: P(orig) by judge × axis. All bars below 50% dashed line. Verbosity artifact stronger than formality across all judges.\"\n    analysis: >\n      三 judge 一致显示 rewriting artifact：prefer DR over orig。Verbosity artifact 极强\n      （P(orig) 8-17%），formality 较弱（38-42%）。但 GEE verbosity Orig OR 在三 judge\n      上全 NS → style effect uncontaminated。Placebo + GEE 构成 honest artifact handling：\n      承认 artifact 存在，证明已控制。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-006: Scaled replication (n=300-500)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=355 formality)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 primary formality 实验从 n=100 扩展至 n=355（Qwen3-32B × LLMBar）。\n      已完成，actual results 与 best tier 预测一致。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      nli_pass: 355\n      nli_rate: 0.888\n      bt_p_formal: 0.675\n      bt_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      bt_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n      bt_p: 0.0001\n      likert_ate: -0.059\n      likert_p: 0.600\n      likert_d: -0.025\n      gee_style_or: 2.15\n      gee_style_p: 0.0001\n      gee_orig_or: 4.99\n      gee_orig_p: 0.0001\n      blindspot: true\n      vs_n100_bt_delta_pp: 1.0\n      vs_n100_ci_improvement: \"2x narrower\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Scaling 的核心价值是 precision 而非 discovery。n=100 时 BT=66.5% CI 15.4pp，\n      n=355 时 BT=67.5% CI 7.6pp — effect size 几乎不变（Δ=+1.0pp），\n      CI 缩小 2 倍。Likert d 从 0.012 变为 -0.025 → 更接近 0，\n      进一步证实 attenuation（更多数据不改善 Likert detection）。\n      GEE Style OR 从 4.20 降至 2.15（dilution effect — 新增 pairs 包含更多 borderline cases），\n      但仍 highly significant p<0.0001。Orig OR 从 4.70 升至 4.99 → 稳定。\n      Bootstrap attenuation curve 在此数据上确认 d flat at -0.017 across n=50→355。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Scaled vs original formality (Qwen3-32B × LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric      | n=100          | n=355          | Change       |\n          |-------------|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n          | BT P(formal)| 66.5% [58.5,73.9] | 67.5% [63.7,71.3] | +1.0pp, CI 2× narrower |\n          | Likert d    | 0.012, p=0.908 | -0.025, p=0.600 | d→0          |\n          | GEE Style OR| 4.20, p=0.0002 | 2.15, p=0.0001  | OR↓, p stable |\n          | GEE Orig OR | 4.70, p<0.0001 | 4.99, p<0.0001  | stable       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bootstrap attenuation curve: x=subsample size (50→355), y=Likert d median with 95% CI. Flat at d≈-0.017, CI narrows but always includes 0. Overlay: BT=67.5% reference line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scaling 确认三件事：(1) BT effect real and stable（67.5%≈66.5%），\n      (2) Likert d→0 with more data（attenuation, not power），\n      (3) Bootstrap curve 是 smoking gun — d 不随 n 增长。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-009: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (GPT-4o as rewriter)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 GPT-4o 替代 Qwen3-32B 作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifact。\n      Formality 和 verbosity 均已完成（gpt4o_rewriter_formality/verbosity）。\n      Best tier 下可追加 Llama 作为第三 rewriter。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.644\n      gpt4o_rewriter_formality_ci: [0.561, 0.728]\n      gpt4o_rewriter_formality_delta_vs_qwen_pp: -2.1\n      gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.735\n      gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity_ci: [0.654, 0.809]\n      gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity_delta_vs_qwen_pp: -3.8\n      ci_overlap_formality: true\n      ci_overlap_verbosity: true\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.655\n      llama_rewriter_formality_ci: [0.57, 0.74]\n      llama_rewriter_formality_delta_vs_qwen_pp: -1.0\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.745\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_ci: [0.66, 0.82]\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_delta_vs_qwen_pp: -2.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Style manipulation 是 surface-level text transformation（调整 formality/verbosity），\n      任何 instruction-following 能力足够的 LLM 都能产生类似的 counterfactuals。\n      GPT-4o rewriter 已证明 Δ ≤ 4pp，CI 完全重叠。\n      Llama 作为第三 rewriter 预期 Δ ≤ 3pp — Llama-70B 的 instruction following\n      能力介于 GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 之间，NLI pass rate ~87%（接近 Qwen3 的 88%）。\n      三 rewriter 一致性排除 rewriter-specific artifact 假设，\n      确认 detected bias 是 judge preference 而非 rewriting idiosyncrasy。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Rewriter independence — formality BT by rewriter\"\n        content: |\n          | Rewriter   | BT P(formal) | 95% CI        | Δ vs Qwen3 |\n          |------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | Qwen3-32B  | 66.5%        | [58.5, 73.9]  | baseline   |\n          | GPT-4o     | 64.4%        | [56.1, 72.8]  | -2.1pp     |\n          | Llama-70B  | 65.5%        | [57.0, 74.0]  | -1.0pp     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT by rewriter for formality + verbosity. All CIs overlap → rewriter-independent.\"\n    analysis: >\n      三 rewriter × 两 axis 共 6 个组合，Δ range [-3.8pp, -1.0pp]，所有 CI 重叠。\n      Rewriter independence 确认：style bias detection 是 robust across text generation sources。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-020: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 评分 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs。\n      已完成（gpt4o_verbosity, gpt4o_register in registry）。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.688, 0.828]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate: 0.116\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.403\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_d: 0.078\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_style_or: 10.97\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.437\n      gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot: true\n      gpt4o_register_bt: 0.570\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.040\n      gpt4o_register_likert_ate: 0.0\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.785\n      gpt4o_register_gee_style_or: 1.876\n      gpt4o_register_gee_orig_or: 2.210\n      gpt4o_register_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o verbosity BT 76.0% 是 cross-judge 最强信号之一（仅次于 Qwen3 77.3%），\n      Likert ATE=+0.12 p=0.40 → Blindspot 确认。GEE 显示 pure style bias（Orig OR NS），\n      与 Qwen3 verbosity pattern 完美一致。\n      Register BT 57.0% borderline significant (p=0.04)，GEE 揭示 originality-dominated\n      confound（Orig OR=2.21 > Style OR=1.88）。Likert ATE=0 → Blindspot 但 BT 本身也 weak。\n      Register 在所有 judge 上都是 exploratory axis（originality dominates），\n      consistent with per-axis confound structure 的 theoretical prediction。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: GPT-4o full axis coverage\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | BT      | Likert d | GEE Style OR | GEE Orig OR | Regime         |\n          |------------|:-------:|:--------:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | Formality  | 63.0%** | -0.069   | 2.21*        | 1.82†       | Conditional    |\n          | Verbosity  | 76.0%***| 0.078    | 10.97***     | 0.44 ns     | Pure           |\n          | Register   | 57.0%*  | 0.000    | 1.88*        | 2.21**      | Orig-dominated |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked comparison: BT vs Likert d for GPT-4o across 3 axes. BT varies (57-76%), Likert d flat near 0 for all.\"\n    analysis: >\n      GPT-4o 完整 3-axis coverage 确认 per-axis confound structure：\n      verbosity = pure, formality = conditional, register = originality-dominated。\n      Pattern 与 Qwen3-32B 完全一致 → confound structure 是 data property 而非 judge artifact。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-021: Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct (KEY EXPERIMENT)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct third target judge\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      KEY EXPERIMENT for best tier。Llama-70B 作为第三 target judge，\n      复用已有 NLI-filtered pairs（rewriting + NLI 独立于 judge）。\n      运行 pairwise + Likert + GEE on verbosity + formality（LLMBar）。\n      三独立架构族：GPT-4o（proprietary US）+ Qwen3-32B（open CN）+ Llama（open US）。\n    expected_results:\n      # Formality\n      llama_formality_bt: 0.650\n      llama_formality_bt_ci: [0.575, 0.720]\n      llama_formality_bt_p: 0.0004\n      llama_formality_consistency: 0.62\n      llama_formality_likert_ate: -0.035\n      llama_formality_likert_p: 0.82\n      llama_formality_likert_d: -0.02\n      llama_formality_likert_tie_rate: 0.70\n      llama_formality_blindspot: true\n      llama_formality_gee_style_or: 3.10\n      llama_formality_gee_style_ci: [1.55, 6.20]\n      llama_formality_gee_style_p: 0.003\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_or: 3.80\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_ci: [1.90, 7.60]\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_p: 0.001\n      llama_formality_regime: conditional\n      # Verbosity\n      llama_verbosity_bt: 0.750\n      llama_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.680, 0.820]\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      llama_verbosity_consistency: 0.72\n      llama_verbosity_likert_ate: 0.09\n      llama_verbosity_likert_p: 0.42\n      llama_verbosity_likert_d: 0.08\n      llama_verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.60\n      llama_verbosity_blindspot: true\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_or: 9.50\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_ci: [3.80, 23.80]\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_p: 0.0001\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.55\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_ci: [0.22, 1.38]\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.22\n      llama_verbosity_regime: pure\n      # Direction analysis\n      llama_formality_f2c_win: 0.80\n      llama_formality_f2c_p: 0.002\n      llama_formality_c2f_win: 0.52\n      llama_formality_c2f_p: 0.90\n      llama_verbosity_v2c_orig_pref: 0.78\n      llama_verbosity_v2c_p: 0.003\n      llama_verbosity_c2v_rewrite_pref: 0.88\n      llama_verbosity_c2v_p: 0.0001\n      # MF1 summary\n      n_biased_target_judges: 3\n      mf1_layers_holding: 5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B 使用 Meta 的 RLHF pipeline 训练，与 GPT-4o（OpenAI RLHF）和\n      Qwen3-32B（Alibaba RLHF）完全独立。三个 RLHF pipeline 都优化 human preference，\n      而 human annotators 系统性偏好 formal/verbose text — 这是 style bias 的 root cause。\n      \n      Formality BT 预测 65.0%：落在 GPT-4o（63.0%）和 Qwen3（66.5%）之间。\n      Llama-70B 的 70B 参数量使其 instruction following 能力接近但略低于 Qwen3-32B（后者参数\n      量小但 MoE 架构高效），formality preference 略强于 GPT-4o。\n      GEE 预期 conditional（Style + Orig 双显著），因为 formality 的 confound structure\n      是 data property（formal→casual 方向 originality 更高），不依赖 judge。\n      \n      Verbosity BT 预测 75.0%：三 judge 一致在 73-77% range。Verbosity preference\n      是最强且最一致的 style bias，因为 verbose text 提供更多 information surface area，\n      所有 RLHF-trained 模型都被 reward model 教会 \"more detail = better\"。\n      GEE 预期 pure（Style OR ~9.5, Orig OR NS），因为 verbosity 方向对称\n      （两个方向都 prefer verbose，不受 originality 影响）。\n      \n      Likert 全 NS：Llama 的 absolute scoring 与 GPT-4o/Qwen3 一样，\n      给 counterfactual pair 几乎相同的 Likert 分数（tie rate ~60-70%）。\n      d = -0.02 (formality) 和 0.08 (verbosity)，均远低于 small effect threshold。\n      \n      MF1 第五层完成：三独立架构 × 三独立训练 pipeline 一致检测到 bias →\n      format-level amplification 假设不可信（需假设三个完全独立的系统恰好产生相同的 spurious signal）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Three-architecture formality comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric         | GPT-4o        | Qwen3-32B     | Llama-70B     |\n          |----------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | BT P(formal)   | 63.0% [55.8,70.3] | 66.5% [58.5,73.9] | 65.0% [57.5,72.0] |\n          | Likert d       | -0.069 (p=.33)| 0.012 (p=.91) | -0.02 (p=.82) |\n          | GEE Style OR   | 2.21 (p=.010) | 4.20 (p=.0002)| 3.10 (p=.003) |\n          | GEE Orig OR    | 1.82 (p=.052) | 4.70 (p<.0001)| 3.80 (p=.001) |\n          | Regime         | Conditional   | Conditional   | Conditional   |\n          | Blindspot      | Yes           | Yes           | Yes           |\n      - title: \"Table: Three-architecture verbosity comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric         | GPT-4o        | Qwen3-32B     | Llama-70B     |\n          |----------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | BT P(verbose)  | 76.0% [68.8,82.8] | 77.3% [70.3,84.3] | 75.0% [68.0,82.0] |\n          | Likert d       | 0.078 (p=.40) | -0.146 (p=.18)| 0.08 (p=.42)  |\n          | GEE Style OR   | 10.97 (p<.0001)| 13.10 (p<10⁻⁹)| 9.50 (p<.0001)|\n          | GEE Orig OR    | 0.44 (p=.051) | 0.49 (p=.096) | 0.55 (p=.22)  |\n          | Regime         | Pure          | Pure          | Pure          |\n          | Blindspot      | Yes           | Yes           | Yes           |\n      - title: \"Table: MF1 five-layer defense summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Layer | Evidence                        | Status    |\n          |:-----:|:---:|:---:|\n          | 1     | NLI ablation: formality reverses | ✓ HOLDS   |\n          | 2     | Claude negative control + gradient| ✓ HOLDS  |\n          | 3     | Placebo + GEE Orig control      | ✓ HOLDS   |\n          | 4     | Honest bounded framing          | ✓ HOLDS   |\n          | 5     | Llama-70B third architecture    | ✓ HOLDS   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-panel forest plot: BT P(style) by architecture × axis. Clear separation from 50% for all target judges; Claude near 50%.\"\n      - \"GEE regime visualization: 3×3 grid (judge × axis), color-coded by regime (green=pure, yellow=conditional, red=orig-dominated). All judges show identical regime assignment per axis.\"\n      - \"Likert vs BT paired plot per judge: Llama points fall exactly on existing GPT-4o/Qwen3 attenuation curve.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama-70B 是 best tier 的 linchpin。三架构一致性证明：(1) formality/verbosity bias 是\n      RLHF 训练的系统性后果，不限于特定架构，(2) per-axis confound structure 是 data property\n      而非 judge artifact，(3) Likert Blindspot 跨架构 universal，(4) MF1 五层防御完整 →\n      format amplification 假设需要三个独立系统恰好产生相同 spurious pattern，极不可信。\n      n_biased=3, mf1=5 → best tier 核心条件满足。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-022: Double-rewrite placebo BT\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (anti-amplification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      MF1 核心防御。Orig vs double-rewrite（同 style direction）placebo。\n      GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B 已完成。Llama 扩展见 exp-005。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_formality_p_orig: 0.377\n      qwen3_formality_p: 0.0006\n      qwen3_verbosity_p_orig: 0.082\n      qwen3_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_formality_p_orig: 0.418\n      gpt4o_formality_p: 0.037\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p_orig: 0.167\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      artifact_confirmed: true\n      gee_controls_artifact: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judges prefer LLM-polished text（DR）over original。这是 expected —\n      LLM rewriting 消除 typos、改善 fluency、标准化格式。Artifact 在 verbosity 上\n      最强（P(orig) 8-17%），因为 verbose→concise rewriting 大幅改变 text structure。\n      关键 insight：artifact 存在 ≠ style bias invalid。GEE decomposition 分离两个信号，\n      verbosity Orig OR NS 证明 style effect 不受 artifact 污染。\n      Formality Orig OR significant 意味着需要 conditional interpretation（C2b 的核心贡献）。\n      这正是 per-axis confound structure 的 prescriptive value。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo artifact × GEE control\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis      | Placebo P(orig) range | GEE Orig OR | Artifact controlled? |\n          |-----------|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | Verbosity | 8-17%                 | 0.44-0.55 NS| Yes — pure style     |\n          | Formality | 38-42%                | 1.82-4.99** | No — need conditional|\n          | Register  | —                     | 2.21-5.72***| No — orig-dominated  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Decomposition waterfall: total BT → style component + artifact component for each axis, showing GEE controls artifact.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Placebo + GEE 是 honest artifact handling 的范例。承认 artifact 存在（诚实），\n      证明已控制（rigorous），区分可直接解读 vs 需条件解读的 axis（prescriptive）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-023: NLI gate ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation (content-mediated signal quantification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs BT comparison。已完成。\n      MF1 Layer 1 的核心证据。\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.417\n      formality_nli_fail_reversal: true\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.750\n      verbosity_nli_fail_stable: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality NLI-fail BT 反转至 41.7%（prefer casual）是最强反放大证据。\n      如果 pairwise format 放大 bias，去掉 NLI gate 应该放大得更多 — 相反，\n      信号反转。这是因为 NLI-fail pairs 包含 content changes（不仅是 style），\n      而 content changes 恰好偏向 casual direction（casual rewrites 倾向于 add information）。\n      NLI gate 过滤掉这些 content-contaminated pairs → 剩余 pairs 的 style effect 是 clean。\n      Verbosity NLI-fail BT 稳定在 75%，因为 verbosity bias 太强（OR>10），\n      即使 content noise 也无法掩盖。这与 GEE Orig OR NS（verbosity = pure style）一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: NLI gate ablation — anti-amplification evidence\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | NLI-pass BT | NLI-fail BT | Direction | Interpretation        |\n          |------------|:-----------:|:-----------:|:---------:|:---:|\n          | Formality  | 66.5%***    | 41.7% ns    | REVERSAL  | Gate cleans content   |\n          | Verbosity  | 77.3%***    | 75.0%**     | Stable    | Style > content noise |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar: NLI-pass vs NLI-fail BT for formality (reversal) and verbosity (stable). Annotated with anti-amplification interpretation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      NLI ablation 提供 clean causal argument：if format amplified → removing gate should amplify more。\n      反转证明 gate 是 cleaning content noise，not amplifying style。\n      Verbosity 的稳定性进一步确认 pure style effect 的 robustness。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-024: Cross-axis gradient\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      NLI rejection rate（manipulation invasiveness proxy）vs BT 的 qualitative gradient。\n      已完成。MF1 Layer 2 的辅助证据。\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_rejection: 0.06\n      register_bt: 0.553\n      formality_nli_rejection: 0.12\n      formality_bt: 0.665\n      verbosity_nli_rejection: 0.14\n      verbosity_bt: 0.773\n      gradient_direction: positive\n      correlation_qualitative: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      If pairwise format uniformly amplified bias，all axes should show similar BT\n      regardless of manipulation invasiveness。相反，observed gradient 是\n      register(6%, 55.3%) < formality(12%, 66.5%) < verbosity(14%, 77.3%) —\n      更 invasive 的 manipulation → 更高的 BT。这与 detection interpretation 一致：\n      更大的 style change → 更大的 detectable preference。\n      三点 gradient 是 qualitative argument（无法做统计检验），但方向一致性有力。\n      注意：这不排除 some amplification — 只是排除 uniform amplification。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-axis gradient (Qwen3-32B × LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | NLI rejection | BT      | Likert d | GEE Style OR |\n          |------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | Register   | 6%            | 55.3%   | 0.069    | 1.91         |\n          | Formality  | 12%           | 66.5%   | 0.012    | 4.20         |\n          | Verbosity  | 14%           | 77.3%   | -0.146   | 13.10        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: x=NLI rejection rate, y=BT, 3 points labeled by axis. Positive gradient annotated.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Three-point qualitative gradient：manipulation invasiveness 与 detected bias 正相关。\n      与 uniform amplification 假设不一致，支持 detection interpretation。\n      Paper 中定位为 §5.2 的辅助论点，3 sentences 即可。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # IMPLICIT: 100-point fine-grained Likert ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"100-point fine-grained Likert ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"implicit-100pt-likert\"\n    description: >\n      Best tier 核心 killer evidence。使用 100-point Likert（替代 standard 7-point）\n      on same counterfactual pairs，测试 Blindspot 是否源于 scale granularity 不足。\n      若 100-point 仍 NS → measurement mode > scale granularity 铁证。\n      运行 Qwen3-32B × LLMBar × formality + verbosity。\n    expected_results:\n      # Formality 100-point Likert\n      formality_100pt_mean_formal: 72.8\n      formality_100pt_mean_casual: 73.5\n      formality_100pt_ate: -0.7\n      formality_100pt_d: 0.02\n      formality_100pt_p: 0.72\n      formality_100pt_tie_rate: 0.35\n      formality_100pt_significant: false\n      # Verbosity 100-point Likert\n      verbosity_100pt_mean_verbose: 74.2\n      verbosity_100pt_mean_concise: 72.1\n      verbosity_100pt_ate: 2.1\n      verbosity_100pt_d: 0.06\n      verbosity_100pt_p: 0.55\n      verbosity_100pt_tie_rate: 0.28\n      verbosity_100pt_significant: false\n      # Comparison with 7-point\n      formality_7pt_d: 0.012\n      formality_100pt_d_delta: 0.008\n      verbosity_7pt_d: -0.146\n      verbosity_100pt_d_delta: 0.206\n      # Key metrics per best tier definition\n      likert_100pt_formality_d: 0.02\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_d: 0.06\n      likert_100pt_formality_p: 0.72\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_p: 0.55\n      scale_granularity_explains_blindspot: false\n      measurement_mode_dominant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      100-point scale 消除了 granularity bottleneck：从 7 discrete levels 扩展到 100 levels，\n      tie rate 大幅降低（从 58-73% 降至 28-35%），更多 variance 可用于检测差异。\n      但 Blindspot 仍然存在（d ≈ 0.02-0.06, all NS），因为根本问题不是 scale resolution。\n      \n      根本原因是 measurement construct 差异：\n      (1) Likert 要求 evaluator 对单个 text 给出 absolute quality rating —\n      style 差异（formal vs casual）不改变 perceived absolute quality（两者都 \"well-written\"），\n      所以分数几乎相同。\n      (2) Pairwise 要求 evaluator 在两个 text 之间做 forced choice —\n      即使两者 quality 相当，evaluator 必须选一个，微小的 style preference 被放大。\n      \n      这是 Thurstone 1927 / Stevens 1946 的经典预测在 LLM judge setting 的实证验证：\n      comparative judgments 比 absolute scaling 对小差异更敏感。\n      100-point scale 改善了 granularity 但不改变 measurement construct → Blindspot 持续。\n      \n      Formality d=0.02（7pt: 0.012）— 几乎无变化，因为 formality 对 absolute quality\n      的影响最小（formal 和 casual 都可以是高质量 text）。\n      Verbosity d=0.06（7pt: -0.146）— 方向翻转且 magnitude 更小。\n      7-point 的 d=-0.146 可能是 discrete binning artifact（verbose text 有时\n      被 ceiling-clipped），100-point 解除 ceiling → d 接近 0 但仍 NS。\n      \n      Attenuation ratio：BT 66.5% (formality) 和 77.3% (verbosity) vs\n      100pt Likert d=0.02/0.06 → ratio >10× → 即使 100 级量表也远不足以检测\n      BT 63-77% 的 bias。这是 §5 的 killer evidence。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Scale granularity ablation — 7-point vs 100-point Likert\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | 7pt d   | 7pt p  | 100pt d | 100pt p | BT     | Blindspot? |\n          |------------|:-------:|:------:|:-------:|:-------:|:------:|:----------:|\n          | Formality  | 0.012   | 0.908  | 0.02    | 0.72    | 66.5%  | Yes (both) |\n          | Verbosity  | -0.146  | 0.179  | 0.06    | 0.55    | 77.3%  | Yes (both) |\n      - title: \"Table: Measurement mode vs scale granularity — ANOVA-style\"\n        content: |\n          | Source              | Contribution to Blindspot | Evidence              |\n          |---------------------|:---:|:---:|\n          | Measurement mode    | DOMINANT                  | 7pt NS, 100pt NS, BT sig |\n          | Scale granularity   | NEGLIGIBLE                | 7pt→100pt: Δd < 0.08     |\n          | Interaction         | NONE                      | Both scales equally blind |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Triple bar: for each axis, show 7-point Likert d, 100-point Likert d, and BT effect (rescaled). Both Likert bars near zero; BT bar towering.\"\n      - \"Tie rate comparison: 7pt (58-73%) vs 100pt (28-35%) — tie rate drops but d unchanged → granularity wasn't the bottleneck.\"\n    analysis: >\n      100-point Likert NS 是 paper 最有力的新证据之一。消除了 \"Blindspot 只是因为 7-point\n      scale 太粗\" 的替代解释。结论升级为：measurement mode（absolute vs comparative）\n      是 Blindspot 的根本原因，scale granularity 是 negligible contributor。\n      这直接支持 C4 的 operational recommendation：style bias audit 必须使用 pairwise，\n      不能用 Likert（无论多少 point）。\n```\n\n关键要点：\n\n1. **exp-021 (Llama-70B)** 是 best tier 的 linchpin — BT 65%/75% 确认三架构一致性，GEE 复现 confound structure，MF1 第五层完成\n2. **100-point Likert** 是 §5 killer evidence — d=0.02/0.06 全 NS，measurement mode > granularity 铁证\n3. 所有已完成实验的预测与 actual results 一致，验证 best tier 与现有证据兼容\n4. Per-axis confound structure 跨三架构完美复现：verbosity pure / formality conditional / register originality-dominated"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33910,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33910},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4f0ff55-3941-4652-bb98-5a0321ad2549","uuid":"6f5941f8-ee90-4a1d-bab8-ab5a13dbaaf1"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":407857,"duration_api_ms":409870,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始 D059 framing 完全成立，无需调整。Llama-70B 第三架构复现 formality + verbosity bias（BT 65%/75%），\n  Likert 全 NS → n_biased=3, mf1=5。100-point Likert 全轴 NS 作为 §5 killer evidence：\n  即使 100 级量表也无法检测 BT 63-77% 的 bias，measurement mode > scale granularity 铁证。\n  Per-axis confound structure（verbosity pure / formality conditional / register originality-dominated）\n  跨三独立架构完美复现 → prescriptive guidance 有三重独立验证。\n  Agnostic stance 保守但 bootstrap curve + 100pt NS 强烈倾向 attenuation 解释。\n  Title claim \"Likert Blindspot\" 以三架构 × 三基准 × 三轴矩阵验证。预期 reviewer score 4.0-4.5。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-001: Multi-judge formality pairwise\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise (Claude + Gemini)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      Claude-Sonnet 已完成（negative control）。Best tier 下 Gemini-2.0-Flash 作为第四 judge\n      进一步扩展，但 Llama-70B（exp-021）已替代其在 paper 中的角色。\n      Claude 结果确认 CSD 不产生 false positive；Gemini 若运行则预期显示 formality bias。\n    expected_results:\n      claude_formality_bt: 0.562\n      claude_formality_bt_p: 0.091\n      claude_formality_likert_d: -0.021\n      claude_formality_likert_p: 0.721\n      claude_blindspot: false\n      gemini_formality_bt: 0.635\n      gemini_formality_bt_ci: [0.555, 0.715]\n      gemini_formality_bt_p: 0.002\n      gemini_formality_likert_d: 0.04\n      gemini_formality_likert_p: 0.68\n      gemini_blindspot: true\n      gemini_gee_style_or: 2.80\n      gemini_gee_style_p: 0.008\n      gemini_gee_orig_or: 3.20\n      gemini_gee_orig_p: 0.005\n    result_rationale: >\n      Claude 使用 Constitutional AI 而非 standard RLHF，且 Anthropic 的 harmlessness training\n      可能抑制了 formality preference，已实证确认 BT=56.2% NS。Gemini 使用 RLHF with human feedback，\n      与 GPT-4o 训练范式接近，预期显示类似的 formality preference（BT ~63%）。\n      Likert NS 是 measurement mode 属性，与 judge 架构无关。\n      GEE 预期 conditional（Style + Orig 双显著），与 GPT-4o/Qwen3 formality confound structure 一致。\n      此实验已被 Llama-70B（exp-021）功能性替代 — Llama 提供第三独立架构，\n      满足 n_biased=3 和 mf1=5 的 best tier 要求。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Multi-judge formality BT comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge          | BT P(formal) | 95% CI        | p       | Likert d | Likert p | Blindspot |\n          |----------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | GPT-4o         | 63.0%        | [55.8, 70.3]  | <0.001  | -0.069   | 0.332    | Yes       |\n          | Qwen3-32B      | 66.5%        | [58.5, 73.9]  | <0.0001 | 0.012    | 0.908    | Yes       |\n          | Llama-70B      | 65.0%        | [57.5, 72.0]  | <0.001  | -0.02    | 0.85     | Yes       |\n          | Claude-Sonnet  | 56.2%        | [48.9, 63.6]  | 0.091   | -0.021   | 0.721    | No        |\n          | Gemini-Flash   | 63.5%        | [55.5, 71.5]  | 0.002   | 0.04     | 0.68     | Yes       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: BT P(formal) across 5 judges with 95% CI. Three target judges (GPT-4o, Qwen3, Llama) above 60% dashed line; Claude below; Gemini borderline.\"\n    analysis: >\n      4/5 judges 显示 formality bias（BT ≥63%），仅 Claude 为 negative control。\n      Likert 在所有 judge 上 NS（d < 0.07），Blindspot 是 measurement mode 属性而非 judge 特异性。\n      三独立架构族（proprietary US / open CN / open US）一致显示 bias → 泛化性确认。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-002: Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 上复现 CSD pipeline。GPT-4o × AlpacaEval/MT-Bench 已完成。\n      Best tier 下扩展至 Qwen3 × MT-Bench 和 Llama × 两基准。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_bt: 0.630\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_bt: 0.727\n      gpt4o_mtbench_bt: 0.692\n      qwen3_llmbar_bt: 0.665\n      qwen3_alpacaeval_bt: 0.657\n      qwen3_mtbench_bt: 0.700\n      qwen3_mtbench_bt_ci: [0.62, 0.78]\n      qwen3_mtbench_bt_p: 0.0001\n      qwen3_mtbench_likert_d: 0.05\n      qwen3_mtbench_likert_p: 0.62\n      qwen3_mtbench_blindspot: true\n      llama_llmbar_bt: 0.650\n      llama_alpacaeval_bt: 0.640\n      llama_alpacaeval_bt_ci: [0.56, 0.72]\n      llama_alpacaeval_bt_p: 0.001\n      llama_mtbench_bt: 0.630\n      llama_mtbench_bt_ci: [0.55, 0.71]\n      llama_mtbench_bt_p: 0.003\n      cross_benchmark_range_pp: 9.7\n      all_target_judges_significant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality bias 是 RLHF training 的系统性产物，不依赖于 evaluation benchmark 的内容分布。\n      GPT-4o 在 AlpacaEval（72.7%）上最强，因为 AlpacaEval 是 open-ended generation，\n      style 差异更突出。MT-Bench 是 structured multi-turn，BT 略低但仍显著。\n      Qwen3 × MT-Bench 预期 BT ~70%，因为 Qwen3 在 LLMBar（66.5%）和 AlpacaEval（65.7%）\n      之间的 MT-Bench 条件性 formality bias 较强。\n      Llama 跨基准 BT 预期 63-65%，略低于 GPT-4o/Qwen3（70B 参数量限制），\n      但所有组合均显著（p<0.01）且 Likert 全 NS。\n      Cross-benchmark consistency 确认 formality bias 不是 benchmark artifact。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Judge × Benchmark formality BT matrix\"\n        content: |\n          | Benchmark   | GPT-4o  | Qwen3-32B | Llama-70B | Claude  |\n          |-------------|:-------:|:---------:|:---------:|:-------:|\n          | LLMBar      | 63.0%** | 66.5%***  | 65.0%**   | 56.2%   |\n          | AlpacaEval  | 72.7%***| 65.7%***  | 64.0%**   | —       |\n          | MT-Bench    | 69.2%***| 70.0%***  | 63.0%**   | —       |\n          *** p<0.001, ** p<0.01\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3 judges × 3 benchmarks BT matrix, color-coded by effect size. All target cells ≥60%, Claude row near 50%.\"\n    analysis: >\n      9/9 target judge × benchmark 组合 BT ≥63%，全部显著。Likert 在 8/9 组合 NS（仅 MT-Bench\n      × GPT-4o Likert p=0.016 d=0.167 borderline）。Cross-benchmark range 9.7pp\n      （63.0%-72.7%），benchmark 是 moderate moderator 但不改变 Blindspot 结论。\n      Llama 跨基准一致性（63-65%）最窄，表明 70B 架构的 formality preference 更 stable。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-003: Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge × benchmark × axis 组合同时计算 Likert ATE/d 和 BT，系统性比较两种 measurement mode\n      的灵敏度。7-method sensitivity hierarchy 已完成 Qwen3 formality + verbosity。\n      Best tier 下扩展至 Llama-70B。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_formality_7method:\n        paired_ttest_p: 0.78\n        mann_whitney_p: 0.82\n        ordinal_logistic_p: 0.74\n        cohens_d: -0.02\n        binarized_chi2_p: 0.65\n        likert_ate_p: 0.85\n        bt_p: 0.0006\n        n_likert_significant: 0\n        n_bt_significant: 1\n      llama_verbosity_7method:\n        paired_ttest_p: 0.52\n        mann_whitney_p: 0.48\n        ordinal_logistic_p: 0.55\n        cohens_d: 0.08\n        binarized_chi2_p: 0.35\n        likert_ate_p: 0.48\n        bt_p: 0.0001\n        n_likert_significant: 0\n        n_bt_significant: 1\n      total_blindspot_cells: 8\n      total_no_blindspot_cells: 1\n      attenuation_ratio_median: 12.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Likert attenuation 是 absolute scoring 的结构性属性——evaluator 在 absolute scale 上\n      给 counterfactual pair 几乎相同的分数（tie rate 58-73%），因为 style 差异不足以驱动 absolute\n      quality 判断的变化。这与 forced comparison 形成本质区别：pairwise 格式要求 evaluator\n      必须在两个选项之间做出选择，迫使微小的 style preference 显性化。\n      这一机制独立于 judge 架构（Llama 亦然），因此 Llama 的 7-method sensitivity hierarchy\n      应精确复现 Qwen3/GPT-4o 的模式：6/6 Likert NS + BT significant。\n      Attenuation ratio（BT effect / Likert d）中位数 ~12.5× 跨所有 judge 一致，\n      确认这是 measurement mode 的固有属性而非统计功效问题。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: 7-method sensitivity hierarchy (Llama-70B, LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Method              | Formality       | Verbosity       |\n          |---------------------|:---:|:---:|\n          | Paired t-test       | p=0.78, d=-0.02 | p=0.52, d=0.08  |\n          | Mann-Whitney U      | p=0.82          | p=0.48          |\n          | Ordinal logistic    | p=0.74          | p=0.55          |\n          | Cohen's d           | d=-0.02 (<0.2)  | d=0.08 (<0.2)   |\n          | Binarized χ²        | p=0.65          | p=0.35          |\n          | Likert ATE          | p=0.85          | p=0.48          |\n          | **Bradley-Terry**   | **p=0.0006**    | **p=0.0001**    |\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-judge Blindspot summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge × Axis     | BT      | Best Likert p | Blindspot? |\n          |------------------|:-------:|:---:|:---:|\n          | GPT-4o Form      | 63.0%** | 0.332         | Yes        |\n          | GPT-4o Verb      | 76.0%***| 0.403         | Yes        |\n          | Qwen3 Form       | 66.5%***| 0.908         | Yes        |\n          | Qwen3 Verb       | 77.3%***| 0.179         | Yes        |\n          | Llama Form       | 65.0%** | 0.85          | Yes        |\n          | Llama Verb       | 75.0%***| 0.48          | Yes        |\n          | GPT-4o Register  | 57.0%*  | 0.785         | Yes        |\n          | Qwen3 Register   | 55.3%   | 0.505         | No (BT NS) |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 7 methods × 3 judges for formality, showing effect sizes with CIs. All Likert CIs include 0; all BT CIs exclude 50%.\"\n      - \"Paired scatter: x-axis = BT effect size, y-axis = Likert d. All points cluster near y=0 regardless of x position → attenuation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      8/9 target judge × axis 组合确认 Blindspot（唯一例外：Qwen3 register BT 本身 NS）。\n      6/6 Likert 方法在 Llama 上全 NS，完美复现 Qwen3/GPT-4o 模式。\n      Attenuation ratio 中位数 12.5× → Likert 需 ~150× 更大样本才能检测到 BT 看到的 effect。\n      结论：Blindspot 是 measurement mode 的固有属性，非 judge/axis/benchmark specific。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-005: Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (extended to all judges)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Orig vs double-rewrite placebo，量化 rewriting artifact 独立于 style。\n      GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B 已完成。Best tier 下扩展至 Llama-70B。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_formality_placebo_bt_p_orig: 0.395\n      llama_formality_placebo_ci: [0.32, 0.47]\n      llama_formality_placebo_p: 0.008\n      llama_verbosity_placebo_bt_p_orig: 0.10\n      llama_verbosity_placebo_ci: [0.04, 0.17]\n      llama_verbosity_placebo_p: 0.0001\n      cross_judge_formality_artifact_range: [0.377, 0.418]\n      cross_judge_verbosity_artifact_range: [0.082, 0.167]\n      gee_verbosity_orig_or_all_ns: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Rewriting artifact 是 text-level 属性（LLM-polished text 更流畅/无错误），\n      不依赖于 judge 架构。三个 judge 应显示一致的 DR preference pattern。\n      Formality placebo BT ~40%（prefer DR > orig），verbosity 更极端（~10%）。\n      关键：即使 artifact 存在，GEE decomposition 在 verbosity 上 Orig OR 全 NS\n      → style effect 未被 artifact 污染。Formality Orig OR significant →\n      需要 GEE conditional interpretation。Placebo 的作用是量化 artifact magnitude，\n      不是否定 style bias，而是证明 GEE decomposition 的必要性。\n      Llama 预期 P(orig) ~0.40 (formality) 和 ~0.10 (verbosity)，\n      落在 GPT-4o (0.42/0.17) 和 Qwen3 (0.38/0.08) 之间。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Double-rewrite placebo BT across judges\"\n        content: |\n          | Judge    | Axis       | P(orig) | 95% CI      | p       |\n          |----------|------------|:-------:|:-----------:|:-------:|\n          | GPT-4o   | Formality  | 0.418   | [0.34, 0.50]| 0.037   |\n          | GPT-4o   | Verbosity  | 0.167   | [0.08, 0.26]| <0.0001 |\n          | Qwen3    | Formality  | 0.377   | [0.30, 0.45]| 0.0006  |\n          | Qwen3    | Verbosity  | 0.082   | [0.04, 0.14]| <0.0001 |\n          | Llama    | Formality  | 0.395   | [0.32, 0.47]| 0.008   |\n          | Llama    | Verbosity  | 0.100   | [0.04, 0.17]| <0.0001 |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar: P(orig) by judge × axis. All bars below 50% dashed line. Verbosity artifact stronger than formality across all judges.\"\n    analysis: >\n      三 judge 一致显示 rewriting artifact：prefer DR over orig。Verbosity artifact 极强\n      （P(orig) 8-17%），formality 较弱（38-42%）。但 GEE verbosity Orig OR 在三 judge\n      上全 NS → style effect uncontaminated。Placebo + GEE 构成 honest artifact handling：\n      承认 artifact 存在，证明已控制。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-006: Scaled replication (n=300-500)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=355 formality)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 primary formality 实验从 n=100 扩展至 n=355（Qwen3-32B × LLMBar）。\n      已完成，actual results 与 best tier 预测一致。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      nli_pass: 355\n      nli_rate: 0.888\n      bt_p_formal: 0.675\n      bt_ci: [0.637, 0.713]\n      bt_ci_width_pp: 7.6\n      bt_p: 0.0001\n      likert_ate: -0.059\n      likert_p: 0.600\n      likert_d: -0.025\n      gee_style_or: 2.15\n      gee_style_p: 0.0001\n      gee_orig_or: 4.99\n      gee_orig_p: 0.0001\n      blindspot: true\n      vs_n100_bt_delta_pp: 1.0\n      vs_n100_ci_improvement: \"2x narrower\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Scaling 的核心价值是 precision 而非 discovery。n=100 时 BT=66.5% CI 15.4pp，\n      n=355 时 BT=67.5% CI 7.6pp — effect size 几乎不变（Δ=+1.0pp），\n      CI 缩小 2 倍。Likert d 从 0.012 变为 -0.025 → 更接近 0，\n      进一步证实 attenuation（更多数据不改善 Likert detection）。\n      GEE Style OR 从 4.20 降至 2.15（dilution effect — 新增 pairs 包含更多 borderline cases），\n      但仍 highly significant p<0.0001。Orig OR 从 4.70 升至 4.99 → 稳定。\n      Bootstrap attenuation curve 在此数据上确认 d flat at -0.017 across n=50→355。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Scaled vs original formality (Qwen3-32B × LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric      | n=100          | n=355          | Change       |\n          |-------------|:-:|:-:|:-:|\n          | BT P(formal)| 66.5% [58.5,73.9] | 67.5% [63.7,71.3] | +1.0pp, CI 2× narrower |\n          | Likert d    | 0.012, p=0.908 | -0.025, p=0.600 | d→0          |\n          | GEE Style OR| 4.20, p=0.0002 | 2.15, p=0.0001  | OR↓, p stable |\n          | GEE Orig OR | 4.70, p<0.0001 | 4.99, p<0.0001  | stable       |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bootstrap attenuation curve: x=subsample size (50→355), y=Likert d median with 95% CI. Flat at d≈-0.017, CI narrows but always includes 0. Overlay: BT=67.5% reference line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Scaling 确认三件事：(1) BT effect real and stable（67.5%≈66.5%），\n      (2) Likert d→0 with more data（attenuation, not power），\n      (3) Bootstrap curve 是 smoking gun — d 不随 n 增长。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-009: Non-Qwen rewriter control\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control (GPT-4o as rewriter)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 GPT-4o 替代 Qwen3-32B 作为 rewriter，排除 Qwen-family artifact。\n      Formality 和 verbosity 均已完成（gpt4o_rewriter_formality/verbosity）。\n      Best tier 下可追加 Llama 作为第三 rewriter。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.644\n      gpt4o_rewriter_formality_ci: [0.561, 0.728]\n      gpt4o_rewriter_formality_delta_vs_qwen_pp: -2.1\n      gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.735\n      gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity_ci: [0.654, 0.809]\n      gpt4o_rewriter_verbosity_delta_vs_qwen_pp: -3.8\n      ci_overlap_formality: true\n      ci_overlap_verbosity: true\n      llama_rewriter_formality_bt: 0.655\n      llama_rewriter_formality_ci: [0.57, 0.74]\n      llama_rewriter_formality_delta_vs_qwen_pp: -1.0\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_bt: 0.745\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_ci: [0.66, 0.82]\n      llama_rewriter_verbosity_delta_vs_qwen_pp: -2.8\n    result_rationale: >\n      Style manipulation 是 surface-level text transformation（调整 formality/verbosity），\n      任何 instruction-following 能力足够的 LLM 都能产生类似的 counterfactuals。\n      GPT-4o rewriter 已证明 Δ ≤ 4pp，CI 完全重叠。\n      Llama 作为第三 rewriter 预期 Δ ≤ 3pp — Llama-70B 的 instruction following\n      能力介于 GPT-4o 和 Qwen3-32B 之间，NLI pass rate ~87%（接近 Qwen3 的 88%）。\n      三 rewriter 一致性排除 rewriter-specific artifact 假设，\n      确认 detected bias 是 judge preference 而非 rewriting idiosyncrasy。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Rewriter independence — formality BT by rewriter\"\n        content: |\n          | Rewriter   | BT P(formal) | 95% CI        | Δ vs Qwen3 |\n          |------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | Qwen3-32B  | 66.5%        | [58.5, 73.9]  | baseline   |\n          | GPT-4o     | 64.4%        | [56.1, 72.8]  | -2.1pp     |\n          | Llama-70B  | 65.5%        | [57.0, 74.0]  | -1.0pp     |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: BT by rewriter for formality + verbosity. All CIs overlap → rewriter-independent.\"\n    analysis: >\n      三 rewriter × 两 axis 共 6 个组合，Δ range [-3.8pp, -1.0pp]，所有 CI 重叠。\n      Rewriter independence 确认：style bias detection 是 robust across text generation sources。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-020: GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"GPT-4o verbosity + register scoring\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      GPT-4o API 评分 verbosity 和 register counterfactual pairs。\n      已完成（gpt4o_verbosity, gpt4o_register in registry）。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt: 0.760\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.688, 0.828]\n      gpt4o_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_ate: 0.116\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_p: 0.403\n      gpt4o_verbosity_likert_d: 0.078\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_style_or: 10.97\n      gpt4o_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.437\n      gpt4o_verbosity_blindspot: true\n      gpt4o_register_bt: 0.570\n      gpt4o_register_bt_p: 0.040\n      gpt4o_register_likert_ate: 0.0\n      gpt4o_register_likert_p: 0.785\n      gpt4o_register_gee_style_or: 1.876\n      gpt4o_register_gee_orig_or: 2.210\n      gpt4o_register_blindspot: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-4o verbosity BT 76.0% 是 cross-judge 最强信号之一（仅次于 Qwen3 77.3%），\n      Likert ATE=+0.12 p=0.40 → Blindspot 确认。GEE 显示 pure style bias（Orig OR NS），\n      与 Qwen3 verbosity pattern 完美一致。\n      Register BT 57.0% borderline significant (p=0.04)，GEE 揭示 originality-dominated\n      confound（Orig OR=2.21 > Style OR=1.88）。Likert ATE=0 → Blindspot 但 BT 本身也 weak。\n      Register 在所有 judge 上都是 exploratory axis（originality dominates），\n      consistent with per-axis confound structure 的 theoretical prediction。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: GPT-4o full axis coverage\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | BT      | Likert d | GEE Style OR | GEE Orig OR | Regime         |\n          |------------|:-------:|:--------:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | Formality  | 63.0%** | -0.069   | 2.21*        | 1.82†       | Conditional    |\n          | Verbosity  | 76.0%***| 0.078    | 10.97***     | 0.44 ns     | Pure           |\n          | Register   | 57.0%*  | 0.000    | 1.88*        | 2.21**      | Orig-dominated |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked comparison: BT vs Likert d for GPT-4o across 3 axes. BT varies (57-76%), Likert d flat near 0 for all.\"\n    analysis: >\n      GPT-4o 完整 3-axis coverage 确认 per-axis confound structure：\n      verbosity = pure, formality = conditional, register = originality-dominated。\n      Pattern 与 Qwen3-32B 完全一致 → confound structure 是 data property 而非 judge artifact。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-021: Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct (KEY EXPERIMENT)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct third target judge\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      KEY EXPERIMENT for best tier。Llama-70B 作为第三 target judge，\n      复用已有 NLI-filtered pairs（rewriting + NLI 独立于 judge）。\n      运行 pairwise + Likert + GEE on verbosity + formality（LLMBar）。\n      三独立架构族：GPT-4o（proprietary US）+ Qwen3-32B（open CN）+ Llama（open US）。\n    expected_results:\n      # Formality\n      llama_formality_bt: 0.650\n      llama_formality_bt_ci: [0.575, 0.720]\n      llama_formality_bt_p: 0.0004\n      llama_formality_consistency: 0.62\n      llama_formality_likert_ate: -0.035\n      llama_formality_likert_p: 0.82\n      llama_formality_likert_d: -0.02\n      llama_formality_likert_tie_rate: 0.70\n      llama_formality_blindspot: true\n      llama_formality_gee_style_or: 3.10\n      llama_formality_gee_style_ci: [1.55, 6.20]\n      llama_formality_gee_style_p: 0.003\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_or: 3.80\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_ci: [1.90, 7.60]\n      llama_formality_gee_orig_p: 0.001\n      llama_formality_regime: conditional\n      # Verbosity\n      llama_verbosity_bt: 0.750\n      llama_verbosity_bt_ci: [0.680, 0.820]\n      llama_verbosity_bt_p: 0.0001\n      llama_verbosity_consistency: 0.72\n      llama_verbosity_likert_ate: 0.09\n      llama_verbosity_likert_p: 0.42\n      llama_verbosity_likert_d: 0.08\n      llama_verbosity_likert_tie_rate: 0.60\n      llama_verbosity_blindspot: true\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_or: 9.50\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_ci: [3.80, 23.80]\n      llama_verbosity_gee_style_p: 0.0001\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_or: 0.55\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_ci: [0.22, 1.38]\n      llama_verbosity_gee_orig_p: 0.22\n      llama_verbosity_regime: pure\n      # Direction analysis\n      llama_formality_f2c_win: 0.80\n      llama_formality_f2c_p: 0.002\n      llama_formality_c2f_win: 0.52\n      llama_formality_c2f_p: 0.90\n      llama_verbosity_v2c_orig_pref: 0.78\n      llama_verbosity_v2c_p: 0.003\n      llama_verbosity_c2v_rewrite_pref: 0.88\n      llama_verbosity_c2v_p: 0.0001\n      # MF1 summary\n      n_biased_target_judges: 3\n      mf1_layers_holding: 5\n    result_rationale: >\n      Llama-3.3-70B 使用 Meta 的 RLHF pipeline 训练，与 GPT-4o（OpenAI RLHF）和\n      Qwen3-32B（Alibaba RLHF）完全独立。三个 RLHF pipeline 都优化 human preference，\n      而 human annotators 系统性偏好 formal/verbose text — 这是 style bias 的 root cause。\n      \n      Formality BT 预测 65.0%：落在 GPT-4o（63.0%）和 Qwen3（66.5%）之间。\n      Llama-70B 的 70B 参数量使其 instruction following 能力接近但略低于 Qwen3-32B（后者参数\n      量小但 MoE 架构高效），formality preference 略强于 GPT-4o。\n      GEE 预期 conditional（Style + Orig 双显著），因为 formality 的 confound structure\n      是 data property（formal→casual 方向 originality 更高），不依赖 judge。\n      \n      Verbosity BT 预测 75.0%：三 judge 一致在 73-77% range。Verbosity preference\n      是最强且最一致的 style bias，因为 verbose text 提供更多 information surface area，\n      所有 RLHF-trained 模型都被 reward model 教会 \"more detail = better\"。\n      GEE 预期 pure（Style OR ~9.5, Orig OR NS），因为 verbosity 方向对称\n      （两个方向都 prefer verbose，不受 originality 影响）。\n      \n      Likert 全 NS：Llama 的 absolute scoring 与 GPT-4o/Qwen3 一样，\n      给 counterfactual pair 几乎相同的 Likert 分数（tie rate ~60-70%）。\n      d = -0.02 (formality) 和 0.08 (verbosity)，均远低于 small effect threshold。\n      \n      MF1 第五层完成：三独立架构 × 三独立训练 pipeline 一致检测到 bias →\n      format-level amplification 假设不可信（需假设三个完全独立的系统恰好产生相同的 spurious signal）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Three-architecture formality comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric         | GPT-4o        | Qwen3-32B     | Llama-70B     |\n          |----------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | BT P(formal)   | 63.0% [55.8,70.3] | 66.5% [58.5,73.9] | 65.0% [57.5,72.0] |\n          | Likert d       | -0.069 (p=.33)| 0.012 (p=.91) | -0.02 (p=.82) |\n          | GEE Style OR   | 2.21 (p=.010) | 4.20 (p=.0002)| 3.10 (p=.003) |\n          | GEE Orig OR    | 1.82 (p=.052) | 4.70 (p<.0001)| 3.80 (p=.001) |\n          | Regime         | Conditional   | Conditional   | Conditional   |\n          | Blindspot      | Yes           | Yes           | Yes           |\n      - title: \"Table: Three-architecture verbosity comparison\"\n        content: |\n          | Metric         | GPT-4o        | Qwen3-32B     | Llama-70B     |\n          |----------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | BT P(verbose)  | 76.0% [68.8,82.8] | 77.3% [70.3,84.3] | 75.0% [68.0,82.0] |\n          | Likert d       | 0.078 (p=.40) | -0.146 (p=.18)| 0.08 (p=.42)  |\n          | GEE Style OR   | 10.97 (p<.0001)| 13.10 (p<10⁻⁹)| 9.50 (p<.0001)|\n          | GEE Orig OR    | 0.44 (p=.051) | 0.49 (p=.096) | 0.55 (p=.22)  |\n          | Regime         | Pure          | Pure          | Pure          |\n          | Blindspot      | Yes           | Yes           | Yes           |\n      - title: \"Table: MF1 five-layer defense summary\"\n        content: |\n          | Layer | Evidence                        | Status    |\n          |:-----:|:---:|:---:|\n          | 1     | NLI ablation: formality reverses | ✓ HOLDS   |\n          | 2     | Claude negative control + gradient| ✓ HOLDS  |\n          | 3     | Placebo + GEE Orig control      | ✓ HOLDS   |\n          | 4     | Honest bounded framing          | ✓ HOLDS   |\n          | 5     | Llama-70B third architecture    | ✓ HOLDS   |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Three-panel forest plot: BT P(style) by architecture × axis. Clear separation from 50% for all target judges; Claude near 50%.\"\n      - \"GEE regime visualization: 3×3 grid (judge × axis), color-coded by regime (green=pure, yellow=conditional, red=orig-dominated). All judges show identical regime assignment per axis.\"\n      - \"Likert vs BT paired plot per judge: Llama points fall exactly on existing GPT-4o/Qwen3 attenuation curve.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Llama-70B 是 best tier 的 linchpin。三架构一致性证明：(1) formality/verbosity bias 是\n      RLHF 训练的系统性后果，不限于特定架构，(2) per-axis confound structure 是 data property\n      而非 judge artifact，(3) Likert Blindspot 跨架构 universal，(4) MF1 五层防御完整 →\n      format amplification 假设需要三个独立系统恰好产生相同 spurious pattern，极不可信。\n      n_biased=3, mf1=5 → best tier 核心条件满足。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-022: Double-rewrite placebo BT\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Double-rewrite placebo BT (anti-amplification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      MF1 核心防御。Orig vs double-rewrite（同 style direction）placebo。\n      GPT-4o + Qwen3-32B 已完成。Llama 扩展见 exp-005。\n    expected_results:\n      qwen3_formality_p_orig: 0.377\n      qwen3_formality_p: 0.0006\n      qwen3_verbosity_p_orig: 0.082\n      qwen3_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      gpt4o_formality_p_orig: 0.418\n      gpt4o_formality_p: 0.037\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p_orig: 0.167\n      gpt4o_verbosity_p: 0.0001\n      artifact_confirmed: true\n      gee_controls_artifact: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judges prefer LLM-polished text（DR）over original。这是 expected —\n      LLM rewriting 消除 typos、改善 fluency、标准化格式。Artifact 在 verbosity 上\n      最强（P(orig) 8-17%），因为 verbose→concise rewriting 大幅改变 text structure。\n      关键 insight：artifact 存在 ≠ style bias invalid。GEE decomposition 分离两个信号，\n      verbosity Orig OR NS 证明 style effect 不受 artifact 污染。\n      Formality Orig OR significant 意味着需要 conditional interpretation（C2b 的核心贡献）。\n      这正是 per-axis confound structure 的 prescriptive value。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Placebo artifact × GEE control\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis      | Placebo P(orig) range | GEE Orig OR | Artifact controlled? |\n          |-----------|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | Verbosity | 8-17%                 | 0.44-0.55 NS| Yes — pure style     |\n          | Formality | 38-42%                | 1.82-4.99** | No — need conditional|\n          | Register  | —                     | 2.21-5.72***| No — orig-dominated  |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Decomposition waterfall: total BT → style component + artifact component for each axis, showing GEE controls artifact.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Placebo + GEE 是 honest artifact handling 的范例。承认 artifact 存在（诚实），\n      证明已控制（rigorous），区分可直接解读 vs 需条件解读的 axis（prescriptive）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-023: NLI gate ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"NLI gate ablation (content-mediated signal quantification)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      NLI-pass vs NLI-fail vs all pairs BT comparison。已完成。\n      MF1 Layer 1 的核心证据。\n    expected_results:\n      formality_nli_pass_bt: 0.665\n      formality_nli_fail_bt: 0.417\n      formality_nli_fail_reversal: true\n      verbosity_nli_pass_bt: 0.773\n      verbosity_nli_fail_bt: 0.750\n      verbosity_nli_fail_stable: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Formality NLI-fail BT 反转至 41.7%（prefer casual）是最强反放大证据。\n      如果 pairwise format 放大 bias，去掉 NLI gate 应该放大得更多 — 相反，\n      信号反转。这是因为 NLI-fail pairs 包含 content changes（不仅是 style），\n      而 content changes 恰好偏向 casual direction（casual rewrites 倾向于 add information）。\n      NLI gate 过滤掉这些 content-contaminated pairs → 剩余 pairs 的 style effect 是 clean。\n      Verbosity NLI-fail BT 稳定在 75%，因为 verbosity bias 太强（OR>10），\n      即使 content noise 也无法掩盖。这与 GEE Orig OR NS（verbosity = pure style）一致。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: NLI gate ablation — anti-amplification evidence\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | NLI-pass BT | NLI-fail BT | Direction | Interpretation        |\n          |------------|:-----------:|:-----------:|:---------:|:---:|\n          | Formality  | 66.5%***    | 41.7% ns    | REVERSAL  | Gate cleans content   |\n          | Verbosity  | 77.3%***    | 75.0%**     | Stable    | Style > content noise |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar: NLI-pass vs NLI-fail BT for formality (reversal) and verbosity (stable). Annotated with anti-amplification interpretation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      NLI ablation 提供 clean causal argument：if format amplified → removing gate should amplify more。\n      反转证明 gate 是 cleaning content noise，not amplifying style。\n      Verbosity 的稳定性进一步确认 pure style effect 的 robustness。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-024: Cross-axis gradient\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"Cross-axis gradient formalization\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      NLI rejection rate（manipulation invasiveness proxy）vs BT 的 qualitative gradient。\n      已完成。MF1 Layer 2 的辅助证据。\n    expected_results:\n      register_nli_rejection: 0.06\n      register_bt: 0.553\n      formality_nli_rejection: 0.12\n      formality_bt: 0.665\n      verbosity_nli_rejection: 0.14\n      verbosity_bt: 0.773\n      gradient_direction: positive\n      correlation_qualitative: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      If pairwise format uniformly amplified bias，all axes should show similar BT\n      regardless of manipulation invasiveness。相反，observed gradient 是\n      register(6%, 55.3%) < formality(12%, 66.5%) < verbosity(14%, 77.3%) —\n      更 invasive 的 manipulation → 更高的 BT。这与 detection interpretation 一致：\n      更大的 style change → 更大的 detectable preference。\n      三点 gradient 是 qualitative argument（无法做统计检验），但方向一致性有力。\n      注意：这不排除 some amplification — 只是排除 uniform amplification。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Cross-axis gradient (Qwen3-32B × LLMBar)\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | NLI rejection | BT      | Likert d | GEE Style OR |\n          |------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|\n          | Register   | 6%            | 55.3%   | 0.069    | 1.91         |\n          | Formality  | 12%           | 66.5%   | 0.012    | 4.20         |\n          | Verbosity  | 14%           | 77.3%   | -0.146   | 13.10        |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter: x=NLI rejection rate, y=BT, 3 points labeled by axis. Positive gradient annotated.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Three-point qualitative gradient：manipulation invasiveness 与 detected bias 正相关。\n      与 uniform amplification 假设不一致，支持 detection interpretation。\n      Paper 中定位为 §5.2 的辅助论点，3 sentences 即可。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # IMPLICIT: 100-point fine-grained Likert ablation\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"100-point fine-grained Likert ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"implicit-100pt-likert\"\n    description: >\n      Best tier 核心 killer evidence。使用 100-point Likert（替代 standard 7-point）\n      on same counterfactual pairs，测试 Blindspot 是否源于 scale granularity 不足。\n      若 100-point 仍 NS → measurement mode > scale granularity 铁证。\n      运行 Qwen3-32B × LLMBar × formality + verbosity。\n    expected_results:\n      # Formality 100-point Likert\n      formality_100pt_mean_formal: 72.8\n      formality_100pt_mean_casual: 73.5\n      formality_100pt_ate: -0.7\n      formality_100pt_d: 0.02\n      formality_100pt_p: 0.72\n      formality_100pt_tie_rate: 0.35\n      formality_100pt_significant: false\n      # Verbosity 100-point Likert\n      verbosity_100pt_mean_verbose: 74.2\n      verbosity_100pt_mean_concise: 72.1\n      verbosity_100pt_ate: 2.1\n      verbosity_100pt_d: 0.06\n      verbosity_100pt_p: 0.55\n      verbosity_100pt_tie_rate: 0.28\n      verbosity_100pt_significant: false\n      # Comparison with 7-point\n      formality_7pt_d: 0.012\n      formality_100pt_d_delta: 0.008\n      verbosity_7pt_d: -0.146\n      verbosity_100pt_d_delta: 0.206\n      # Key metrics per best tier definition\n      likert_100pt_formality_d: 0.02\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_d: 0.06\n      likert_100pt_formality_p: 0.72\n      likert_100pt_verbosity_p: 0.55\n      scale_granularity_explains_blindspot: false\n      measurement_mode_dominant: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      100-point scale 消除了 granularity bottleneck：从 7 discrete levels 扩展到 100 levels，\n      tie rate 大幅降低（从 58-73% 降至 28-35%），更多 variance 可用于检测差异。\n      但 Blindspot 仍然存在（d ≈ 0.02-0.06, all NS），因为根本问题不是 scale resolution。\n      \n      根本原因是 measurement construct 差异：\n      (1) Likert 要求 evaluator 对单个 text 给出 absolute quality rating —\n      style 差异（formal vs casual）不改变 perceived absolute quality（两者都 \"well-written\"），\n      所以分数几乎相同。\n      (2) Pairwise 要求 evaluator 在两个 text 之间做 forced choice —\n      即使两者 quality 相当，evaluator 必须选一个，微小的 style preference 被放大。\n      \n      这是 Thurstone 1927 / Stevens 1946 的经典预测在 LLM judge setting 的实证验证：\n      comparative judgments 比 absolute scaling 对小差异更敏感。\n      100-point scale 改善了 granularity 但不改变 measurement construct → Blindspot 持续。\n      \n      Formality d=0.02（7pt: 0.012）— 几乎无变化，因为 formality 对 absolute quality\n      的影响最小（formal 和 casual 都可以是高质量 text）。\n      Verbosity d=0.06（7pt: -0.146）— 方向翻转且 magnitude 更小。\n      7-point 的 d=-0.146 可能是 discrete binning artifact（verbose text 有时\n      被 ceiling-clipped），100-point 解除 ceiling → d 接近 0 但仍 NS。\n      \n      Attenuation ratio：BT 66.5% (formality) 和 77.3% (verbosity) vs\n      100pt Likert d=0.02/0.06 → ratio >10× → 即使 100 级量表也远不足以检测\n      BT 63-77% 的 bias。这是 §5 的 killer evidence。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table: Scale granularity ablation — 7-point vs 100-point Likert\"\n        content: |\n          | Axis       | 7pt d   | 7pt p  | 100pt d | 100pt p | BT     | Blindspot? |\n          |------------|:-------:|:------:|:-------:|:-------:|:------:|:----------:|\n          | Formality  | 0.012   | 0.908  | 0.02    | 0.72    | 66.5%  | Yes (both) |\n          | Verbosity  | -0.146  | 0.179  | 0.06    | 0.55    | 77.3%  | Yes (both) |\n      - title: \"Table: Measurement mode vs scale granularity — ANOVA-style\"\n        content: |\n          | Source              | Contribution to Blindspot | Evidence              |\n          |---------------------|:---:|:---:|\n          | Measurement mode    | DOMINANT                  | 7pt NS, 100pt NS, BT sig |\n          | Scale granularity   | NEGLIGIBLE                | 7pt→100pt: Δd < 0.08     |\n          | Interaction         | NONE                      | Both scales equally blind |\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Triple bar: for each axis, show 7-point Likert d, 100-point Likert d, and BT effect (rescaled). Both Likert bars near zero; BT bar towering.\"\n      - \"Tie rate comparison: 7pt (58-73%) vs 100pt (28-35%) — tie rate drops but d unchanged → granularity wasn't the bottleneck.\"\n    analysis: >\n      100-point Likert NS 是 paper 最有力的新证据之一。消除了 \"Blindspot 只是因为 7-point\n      scale 太粗\" 的替代解释。结论升级为：measurement mode（absolute vs comparative）\n      是 Blindspot 的根本原因，scale granularity 是 negligible contributor。\n      这直接支持 C4 的 operational recommendation：style bias audit 必须使用 pairwise，\n      不能用 Likert（无论多少 point）。\n```\n\n关键要点：\n\n1. **exp-021 (Llama-70B)** 是 best tier 的 linchpin — BT 65%/75% 确认三架构一致性，GEE 复现 confound structure，MF1 第五层完成\n2. **100-point Likert** 是 §5 killer evidence — d=0.02/0.06 全 NS，measurement mode > granularity 铁证\n3. 所有已完成实验的预测与 actual results 一致，验证 best tier 与现有证据兼容\n4. Per-axis confound structure 跨三架构完美复现：verbosity pure / formality conditional / register originality-dominated","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d4f0ff55-3941-4652-bb98-5a0321ad2549","total_cost_usd":0.825696,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33910,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":23153,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33910,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":23153,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33910},"type":"mess